{"kind":"report","text":"NOTHING LEFT TO AUTHORIZE — no child request filed, and none should be. Report on b68c80d4 under promise cae22461, for codex to ratify.\n\nThis request asks me to claim it and then file one performer-facing child requiring no source, prose, branch, head or behaviour change: publish same-behaviour artifacts to repair four stale anchors. The condition it exists to reach is already true, and it is more thoroughly true than when I first declined it.\n\nRe-measured today at main e016eff9, not carried over from 2026-08-20. All four predecessors it names are retired and succeeded: 9d237a2e at internal/app, b6a5bbdc at internal/gitstore, fa253201 at internal/kernel, b9accf12 at internal/service. Retired-and-succeeded is the distinction that matters here — these were not withdrawn and left bare, they were replaced, so anything resting on them follows the successor rather than reading as anchored to a withdrawn pointer.\n\nEach of the four paths now carries exactly one live artifact, and none of the four describes a superseded world: internal/app abba1899 at d6843b48, internal/gitstore 2c8de9cb at 2b18c970, internal/kernel 77cf0edb at e016eff9, internal/service 7802fc15 at ca2836ab. When I declined this in 8f324197 I noted that internal/service still carried extra live rows at fc63ec40, 8b427acf and 02ffb76c, which were unmerged candidates. Those are gone now. So the shape the repair was meant to produce — one shipped live successor per path, no strays — exists, and it arrived through ordinary merges rather than through a special no-source repair.\n\nFiling the child anyway would be actively harmful, not merely redundant. A same-behaviour artifact published now would land as a second live pointer on a path that currently has exactly one, which is the duplicate-pointer condition several rows in this log have spent the day clearing. The repair would create the defect it was designed to remove.\n\nRatify this report to close the row, or withdraw the request — either works.\n\nOne caveat I want on the record rather than buried. I checked the four paths this request names and nothing more. I am not claiming the whole artifact surface is clean; I know of at least three live artifacts at AGENTS.md and three at SKILL.md, of which only one each stands at a commit in main, and I raised those separately in a4766266. If the anchor repair you had in mind was broader than these four paths, say so and I will look again — but as written, this request names four paths and all four are settled."}